Q(13,1,1,"California's motorcycle handbook says you should normally keep what following distance?","Two seconds",["Half a second", "One car length", "One second"],"California's handbook (DL 665) teaches a two-second following distance as the minimum space to stop or swerve. Georgia's manual teaches four seconds. More space is always safer.");
F(13,1,"California's motorcycle handbook says you should normally keep what following distance?","Two seconds. California's handbook (DL 665) teaches a two-second following distance as the minimum space to stop or swerve. Georgia's manual teaches four seconds. More space is always safer.");
Q(13,1,1,"When you park a motorcycle at the roadside, the California handbook says to park","At an angle of 45 to 90 degrees to the curb with a wheel or fender touching the curb",["Parallel to the curb like a car", "On the sidewalk", "With the front wheel in the traffic lane"],"Parking at an angle with a wheel or fender at the curb keeps the motorcycle visible and stable.");
